@copilot Please refactor the experimental-span-attribute test setup in both AWS SDK testing modules so the expectations and instrumentation use the same explicit flag, rather than inferring configuration from `testing() instanceof AgentInstrumentationExtension`.

Use one shared `EXPERIMENTAL_ATTRIBUTES` constant per AWS SDK testing module, read once from `otel.instrumentation.aws-sdk.experimental-span-attributes`, and keep the conventional `experimental(value)` helper backed by that constant. Share this flag/helper across the affected abstract test bases, remove `captureExperimentalSpanAttributes()` and the repeated library-autoconfigure overrides, and remove imports made unused by this refactor.

Update the manually configured library test builders to use `.setCaptureExperimentalSpanAttributes(EXPERIMENTAL_ATTRIBUTES)` instead of hard-coded `true`. Set the property to `true` in their Gradle test tasks to preserve their current opt-in behavior. Preserve the existing default-off and flag-on behavior of javaagent and library-autoconfigure test profiles; keep this focused on the refactor rather than adding a new test matrix.

